b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ HARNESS POSING incremental;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE author: implementation-algol-60, an agent (Claude Opus 5.5, claude-opus-5-5);
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE precursor seen: no;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ PROVENANCE idioms: the Revised Report on ALGOL 60 (1962) for blocks and arrays (5.2), procedures and function designators (5.4), the for statement with step-until and while elements (4.6) and conditional statements and expressions (3.3, 4.5), the X1 system's input and output procedures read, print, PRINTTEXT and NLCR, as the harness README gives them (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.1) and its own X1 programs cite them (Kruseman Aretz 2003, chapter 7), and the X1 compiler's representation, with underlined reserved words and the operator symbols (harness README, 2.1), the effect stub emit bound as printing and the replayed commitment read back as an integer (harnesses/algol-60/README.md, 2.2 and 2.5), the message loop and observe block of the harness README example X01 (2.8), and the holding of each relation posed after pick, and of the position reached in pick's facts, written for this problem (METRICS.md, rule 19), with no period source;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ CONSTANTS a line 1: F f1 ... fF, the number of facts of pick and then the value of each fact, in order. Stage 2, commit, has no constants. A line 3: c, the integer of x different from c;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ P11d. One unknown x, and queries for any one outcome. Stage 1: pick(x) and emit(x). Stage 2: commit. Stage 3: x different from c3. pick is given by its facts, tried in order, one at a time: a fact gives x its value, emit(x) is carried out, as the conjunct that follows pick in stage 1, and then every relation posed since is tested, in the order posed. The first fact that passes them all is the outcome reported, and the facts after it are kept, untried. When a later stage refutes the outcome, the next facts are tried in the same way. Commit selects the outcome held and adds the information x = v, held as one more relation. A replayed commitment, the message 3, gives v, which is read back and added in the same way. An answer, and the entry emitted, is x alone, its digits printed with no spaces;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ n, cap, m, i, code, k, j, nf, c3, xv, cur, cv, untried;
  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ picked, xk, committed, r3;
  i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ a̲r̲r̲a̲y̲ fv[1:1000], pk[1:1000];

  b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ holds(x);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ x; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ x;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the relations posed after pick(x) and emit(x), tested on x in the order posed: x = v, once the commitment is made, and x different from c3, once stage 3 is posed;
  holds := (i̲f̲ committed t̲h̲e̲n̲ x = cv e̲l̲s̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲) ∧ (i̲f̲ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ x ≠ c3 e̲l̲s̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲);

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ num(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ output adapter: an integer, a minus sign if it is negative and then its decimal digits, with no spaces;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ d;
    i̲f̲ v < 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`-'); num(-v) e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      i̲f̲ v ≥ 10 t̲h̲e̲n̲ num(v ÷ 10);
      d := v - v ÷ 10 × 10;
      i̲f̲ d = 0 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`0') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`1') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`2')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`3') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 4 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`4') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 5 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`5')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 6 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`6') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 7 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`7') e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ d = 8 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`8')
      e̲l̲s̲e̲ PRINTTEXT(`9')
    e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲ num;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ emit(v);
    v̲a̲l̲u̲e̲ v; i̲n̲t̲e̲g̲e̲r̲ v;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the effect stub emit(v) of the harness, bound as printing;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[emit]'); num(v); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/emit]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲ emit;

  p̲r̲o̲c̲e̲d̲u̲r̲e̲ advance;
  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the facts of pick after the current one, tried in order until one passes: each gives x its value, emit(x) is carried out, and the relations posed since are tested. If none passes, x has no value;
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    b̲o̲o̲l̲e̲a̲n̲ ok;
    ok := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 0 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ ¬ok ∧ cur < nf d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      cur := cur + 1; pk[cur] := pk[cur] + 1;
      xv := fv[cur];
      emit(xv);
      ok := holds(xv)
    e̲n̲d̲;
    xk := ok
  e̲n̲d̲ advance;

  c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: the instance line;
  n := read; cap := read; m := read;
  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ m d̲o̲ code := read;
  picked := xk := committed := r3 := f̲a̲l̲s̲e̲; nf := cur := 0;

  f̲o̲r̲ i := 1 w̲h̲i̲l̲e̲ t̲r̲u̲e̲ d̲o̲
  b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ harness words: one message, the stage it poses, replays or replays as a commitment, and then, for a commitment, its value v;
    code := read; k := read;
    i̲f̲ code = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the replayed commit stage, as the information x = v;
      cv := read; committed := t̲r̲u̲e̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 1 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ pick(x) and emit(x): pick's facts, then the first of them;
      nf := read;
      f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ fv[j] := read; pk[j] := 0 e̲n̲d̲;
      picked := t̲r̲u̲e̲; cur := 0;
      advance
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 2 t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ commit: the outcome held is selected, and x = v is added;
      i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ cv := xv; committed := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲
    e̲l̲s̲e̲ i̲f̲ k = 3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ c3 := read; r3 := t̲r̲u̲e̲ e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the outcome held, if a relation posed at this stage refutes it, is replaced by the next fact that passes;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ ¬holds(xv) t̲h̲e̲n̲ advance e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ the answer: the one outcome held;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[answer]'); num(xv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/answer]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;

    c̲o̲m̲m̲e̲n̲t̲ observe: the outcome, the relations held, the commitment, the facts of pick tried and untried;
    untried := i̲f̲ picked t̲h̲e̲n̲ nf - cur e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0;
    PRINTTEXT(`[observe]');
    i̲f̲ picked ∧ ¬xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`no solution'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[bind x]'); num(xv); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/bind]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    PRINTTEXT(`relations after pick and emit: ');
    i̲f̲ ¬committed ∧ ¬r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`none');
    i̲f̲ committed t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`x = '); num(cv); PRINTTEXT(` (committed)') e̲n̲d̲;
    i̲f̲ r3 t̲h̲e̲n̲ b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ i̲f̲ committed t̲h̲e̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`, '); PRINTTEXT(`not (x = '); num(c3); PRINTTEXT(`)') e̲n̲d̲;
    NLCR;
    i̲f̲ picked t̲h̲e̲n̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲
      PRINTTEXT(`facts of pick tried: '); num(cur); PRINTTEXT(` of '); num(nf);
      PRINTTEXT(`, untried and kept for a later stage: '); num(untried); NLCR;
      b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[held-as backtracking]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲;
      PRINTTEXT(`[problem-alternatives x '); print((i̲f̲ xk t̲h̲e̲n̲ 1 e̲l̲s̲e̲ 0) + untried); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲
    e̲n̲d̲;
    f̲o̲r̲ j := 1 s̲t̲e̲p̲ 1 u̲n̲t̲i̲l̲ nf d̲o̲
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[operations pick/'); num(j); PRINTTEXT(` '); print(pk[j]); b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`]'); NLCR e̲n̲d̲ e̲n̲d̲;
    b̲e̲g̲i̲n̲ PRINTTEXT(`[/observe]'); NLCR; PRINTTEXT(`[end]') e̲n̲d̲
  e̲n̲d̲
e̲n̲d̲
